
    __init__.py     // <empty>
    loader.hy       // DEF: load_fpmx (macro)
    lenses.hy       // • import lenses [lens]                                                  require [lns ...] ←┐
                                                                                                                  |
    /prelude |                                                                                                    |
             | __init__.py           //  ┌→ import * , require * ←——————————————————————┐                         |
             | __init__macros.hy     //  |                       ┌→ require (+minidoc) →•← require (+minidoc) ←┐  |
             | funcs.hy              //  • ⁺FUNCS_fpmx           |                                             |  |
             | macros.hy             //     (def+minidoc+docstr) • ¹MACRO_fpmx                                 |  • ³MACRO_lns
             | from_hyrule.hy        //                                                  ²MACRO_hyrule_replica • 

    /strict  | types.hy              // StrictInt, validateF, etc.
             | maybeM.hy   
             | resultM.hy  

    /monads  | maybeM.hy   
             | resultM.hy  

	/term	 | ...

    ·····························································································

    • load_fpmx is in loader.hy (instead of __init__.py) because
      this way «import fpmx.prelude *» is faster

    • python calls hy.eval(hy.read(...)) are expensive
    • 1000 same «imports» are free, 1000 same «requires» add up to noticiable startup time

